<title>UK: IEA regrets U.S. plan to sell $209 mln oil stocks.</title>
<headline>IEA regrets U.S. plan to sell $209 mln oil stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robert Priddle, Director of the International Energy Agency (IEA) in Paris, said on Friday he &quot;regrets&quot; the approval of a plan by a U.S. House of Representative's committee to sell $209 million worth of oil from America's Strategic Petroleum Reserve.</p>
</text>
